WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.740
Today's chemical is acetone, CAS number 67-64-1.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:10.120
Acetone is highly flammable and can ignite even at minus 17 degrees Celsius.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.360
Its heavy vapor can travel to a spark and flash back.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:18.740
It causes serious eye irritation, and breathing the vapor may make you dizzy or drowsy.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:24.160
Keep away from heat, sparks and flames. Ground containers and use non-sparking tools.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.370
Work with good ventilation, and store it sealed in a cool, locked area.

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:33.280
Wear goggles and a face shield, chemical-resistant gloves and protective clothing.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.180
If ventilation is poor, wear a gas mask with the right cartridge.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:43.860
Eyes: rinse with running water for 20 minutes. Skin: wash with soap and water. Inhaled: get fresh air.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:47.640
Spill: remove ignition sources and absorb with dry sand.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.190
Fire: use CO2, dry chemical or foam. No direct water jet.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:57.760
On the label, pictograms show the hazard type. The signal word Danger means serious risk.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.560
Hazard statements explain the risk; precautionary statements tell you what to do.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.600
The full MSDS has 16 sections. Check it at your workplace before handling.
